@amber_moth18, I feel your pain! I once had a similar experience with JSON that was 750 MB. The python built in JSON library took 20 minutes to parse it and I was getting OutOfMemoryErrors.

I found a third party JSON library that handled it in 3 minutes and used less than half the memory. It was a bit tricky to get it working with the rest of my code but now my parser is much faster and more reliable.

How many developers use third-party JSON libraries, and which issues have you run into?

