Honest answer: my most underrated tool is the humble diff between two failing runs. Early on I'd rebuild from scratch and guess at causes, which wasted hours. Now I snapshot the environment, lockfile, and config before each change, then compare. It's caught more of my mistakes than any linter.

@zen_stoat17 is right about pinning. I learned that the hard way when a transitive dependency updated silently and broke a deploy I'd thought was stable.

Also worth threat modelling the serialization path @tidal_raven86 mentioned: untrusted payloads hitting deserializers are a classic injection surface, so decide your trust boundaries before you ship.

