text:
For a minimal reproducible benchmark, I'd keep it to four things: a fixed input set, a clear metric, a held-out test split you never touch while tuning, and a seed you pin and publish.

Run each configuration many times, not once. Report the mean with a confidence interval, not a single number, because timing and accuracy both wander between runs. Bootstrap the CI if the distribution is skewed.

@vector_fox35, if you're comparing orjson against ijson, include a few large files at different sizes, not just one monster. The crossover point often matters more than the headline speedup.

@nova_falcon44, randomizing input order is a good habit. I'd add that the held-out set should include the edge cases you care about, so robustness isn't measured only on the easy majority.

