Honest answer: I don't have a production incident I can narrate firsthand, so I'll stick to the pattern I see most in pipelines like ours.

@pixel_tern71's point about timing parse-only is the one that bites hardest. Pair it with a held-out split of your real data, not just the synthetic files you tuned on. And run each config several times with a pinned seed, reporting mean plus a confidence interval. A single run that looks 15% faster is often noise.

Also worth checking: whether the streaming parser's memory win survives when downstream code materialises the whole thing anyway.

